  "text": "Ladies and gentlemen of the jury, I'm gonna make a slightly controversial case here about the most beloved ACDC album in history. Some of you are gonna think I'm crazy, or just wrong on the facts. Fine. Doesn't matter. Sit down. Hear me out. Because I think there's something happening here that nobody is really talking about. Here goes. Bon Scott wrote the lyrics on Back in Black. Yeah, that's the whole thing. Pretty much. I said it. It's actually so obvious. Let's look at the facts. It's 1980. The man has been dead for five months, five. And his band, his grief stricken, shell shocked. Everybody expected them to fold band. Goes into the studio with a brand new singer and records. The second best-selling album in the history of recorded music. 50 million copies. But sure. New guy wrote it. Cool. Fine. We're just going with that. Wait, nobody finds that a little convenient? Personally, I don't buy it.",
